  "liner": {
   "body_md": "## What listeners single out\n\n- **Drink Up And Go Home** (1 other source): David Nelson plays mandolin on this song, which is the only known Grateful Dead performance of it [1]\n- **A Voice From On High** (1 other source): David Nelson plays mandolin and John Dawson sings vocals; it is the only known Grateful Dead performance of the song [1]\n\n## Setlist highlights\n\n- **Tell It To Me**: earliest performance in the archive; rare: 3 archived performances [2]\n- **Drink Up And Go Home**: earliest performance in the archive; mythic rare: 2 archived performances [2]\n- **A Voice From On High**: earliest performance in the archive; rare: 5 archived performances [2]\n- **Swing Low Sweet Chariot**: earliest performance in the archive; rare: 13 archived performances [2]\n- **Deep Elem Blues**: back after 166 archived shows (880 days) [2]\n- **Ballad Of Casey Jones**: earliest performance in the archive; rare: 3 archived performances [2]\n- Earliest performances in the archive: Candyman, El Paso, Rosa Lee McFall, Cold Jordan, Dark Hollow, To Lay Me Down [2]\n\n## The recordings\n\n- **gd1970-01-01.154490.sbd.gems.flac16** (recommended): soundboard; 15 songs; 60 min [1]\n\n## Around the show\n\n- This recording long circulated as August 5, 1970 at Golden Hall, San Diego, but there is no evidence that show happened [1]\n\n## Tapers and lineage\n\n- **gd1970-01-01.154490.sbd.gems.flac16**: source: Source: Restoration of SHNID 017271 Thanks to Joe Jupille and Andy Lemiuex for the original source [1]",
